# Mihomo external-controller API Reference

> Source: [wiki.metacubex.one/en/api](https://wiki.metacubex.one/en/api)  
> Fetched: 2026-10-27  
> Project: `ayatsuri` — `lib/main.dart` `ClashController`

All endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <secret>`.

```
curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer ***' http://${controller-api}/endpoint
```

---

## Version

### `GET /version`

Retrieve mihomo version info.

| Field  | Type             | Description                    |
| ------ | ---------------- | ------------------------------ |
| `meta` | `bool`           | Whether this is a Meta build   |
| `version` | `string`       | Version string                 |

---

## Proxies

### `GET /proxies`

Retrieve all proxy and group information.

Response: `{ "proxies": { "<name>": { … } } }`

**Common fields** (every entry):

| Field            | Type    | Description                                                |
| ---------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| `name`           | string  | Proxy or group name                                        |
| `type`           | string  | `Shadowsocks`, `VMess`, `DIRECT`, `Selector`, `URLTest`, `Fallback`, `LoadBalance`, etc. |
| `udp`            | bool    | Whether UDP is supported                                   |
| `uot`            | bool    | Whether UDP over TCP is supported                          |
| `xudp`           | bool    | Whether XUDP is supported                                  |
| `tfo`            | bool    | Whether TCP Fast Open is enabled                           |
| `mptcp`          | bool    | Whether MPTCP is enabled                                   |
| `smux`           | bool    | Whether stream multiplexing is enabled                     |
| `alive`          | bool    | Whether the proxy is currently alive                       |
| `history`        | array   | Delay history entries, each with `time` and `delay` (ms)   |
| `extra`          | object  | Extra delay histories grouped by test URL                  |
| `interface`      | string  | Bound network interface name                               |
| `routing-mark`   | int     | Routing mark value                                          |
| `provider-name`  | string  | Name of the proxy provider this proxy belongs to           |
| `dialer-proxy`   | string  | Underlying dialer proxy name                                |

**Policy group extra fields** (`Selector`, `URLTest`, `Fallback`, `LoadBalance`):

| Field           | Type    | Description                                                        |
| --------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `now`           | string  | Currently selected node name (absent for `LoadBalance`)           |
| `all`           | array   | Array of all node/group names in the group                         |
| `testUrl`       | string  | Health check URL                                                    |
| `hidden`        | bool    | Whether the group is hidden in the dashboard                       |
| `icon`          | string  | Icon URL                                                            |
| `emptyFallback` | string  | Fallback node name used when all members are unavailable           |
| `expectedStatus`| int     | Expected HTTP response status code for health checks (absent for `Selector`) |
| `fixed`         | string  | Currently pinned node name (only `URLTest` and `Fallback`)         |

### `GET /proxies/<name>`

Retrieve a specific proxy or group.

### `PUT /proxies/<name>`

Select a specific proxy within a policy group.

Body: `{"name": "Japan"}`

Response: HTTP 204

### `DELETE /proxies/<name>`

Clear the fixed selection of the proxy/policy group (except for `Selector` type).

Response: HTTP 204

### `GET /proxies/<name>/delay`

Test a specified proxy and return new delay information.

Query parameters:

| Parameter | Type   | Default                  | Description                                       |
| --------- | ------ | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `url`     | string | (required)               | Test URL                                          |
| `timeout` | int    | 5000                     | Timeout in milliseconds                           |
| `expected`| string | (optional)               | Expected HTTP status code; supports ranges (`200/204`, `200-299`) |

Response: `{ "delay": <uint16> }` (milliseconds)

---

## Policy Groups

### `GET /group`

Retrieve all policy groups.

Response: `{ "proxies": [ { … }, … ] }` (same format as `/proxies/<name>`)

### `GET /group/<name>`

Retrieve a specific policy group.

### `GET /group/<name>/delay`

Test all nodes/strategy groups within the specified strategy group; clears the fixed selection of automatic strategy groups.

Query: `?url=xxx&timeout=5000&expected=xxx`

Response: `{ "<nodeName>": <delay_ms>, … }`

---

## Running Configuration

### `GET /configs`

Retrieve the current running configuration.

Response: JSON object including `port`, `socks-port`, `mixed-port`, `mode`, `log-level`, `allow-lan`, `ipv6`, `tun`, and other fields.

### `PUT /configs`

Reload basic configuration.

Query: `?force=true`

Response: HTTP 204

### `PATCH /configs`

Update a single configuration field.

Body: `{"mixed-port": 7890}`

Response: HTTP 204

### `POST /configs/geo`

Update the GEO database.

Body: `{"path": "", "payload": ""}`

Response: HTTP 204

---

## Cache

### `POST /cache/fakeip/flush`

Clear the fake IP cache.

Response: HTTP 204

### `POST /cache/dns/flush`

Clear the DNS cache.

Response: HTTP 204

---

## Connections

### `GET /connections`

Retrieve active connections. Also available as WebSocket (streaming).

Query: `?interval=<milliseconds>` (default 1000)

Response:

| Field          | Type   | Description                                     |
| -------------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------- |
| `downloadTotal`| int    | Cumulative downloaded bytes                     |
| `uploadTotal`  | int    | Cumulative uploaded bytes                       |
| `memory`       | int    | Current memory usage (bytes)                    |
| `connections`  | array  | Active connection objects:                       |
|                |        | - `id`: unique connection ID                    |
|                |        | - `metadata`: source/dest address, protocol, process |
|                |        | - `upload` / `download`: bytes on this conn     |
|                |        | - `start`: connection start time                |
|                |        | - `chains`: proxy chain array                   |
|                |        | - `providerChains`: provider proxy chain array  |
|                |        | - `rule`: matched rule type                     |
|                |        | - `rulePayload`: matched rule content           |

### `DELETE /connections`

Close all connections.

Response: HTTP 204

### `DELETE /connections/<id>`

Close a specific connection.

Response: HTTP 204

---

## Rules

### `GET /rules`

Retrieve all rules.

Response: `{ "rules": [ { … }, … ] }`

| Field     | Type   | Description                                            |
| --------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| `index`   | int    | Rule index (0-based)                                    |
| `type`    | string | Rule type (`DOMAIN`, `IP-CIDR`, `GEOIP`, etc.)         |
| `payload` | string | Rule match content                                      |
| `proxy`   | string | Target proxy or policy group name                       |
| `size`    | int    | Number of entries in the rule set (only for `GEOIP`/`GEOSITE`, `-1` otherwise) |
| `extra`   | object | Optional: `disabled`, `hitCount`, `hitAt`, `missCount`, `missAt` |

### `PATCH /rules/disable`

Disable rules by index. Temporary; reset after restart.

Body: `{"0": false, "1": true}`

Response: HTTP 204

---

## Proxy Providers

### `GET /providers/proxies`

Retrieve all proxy provider information.

Response: `{ "providers": { "<name>": { … } } }`

### `GET /providers/proxies/<name>`

Retrieve a specific proxy provider.

### `PUT /providers/proxies/<name>`

Update a proxy provider.

Response: HTTP 204

### `GET /providers/proxies/<name>/healthcheck`

Trigger a health check for a proxy provider.

Response: HTTP 204

### `GET /providers/proxies/<name>/proxies/<proxy_name>`

Retrieve a specific proxy within a proxy provider.

### `GET /providers/proxies/<name>/proxies/<proxy_name>/healthcheck`

Test a specified proxy within a proxy provider.

Query: `?url=xxx&timeout=5000`

Response: `{ "delay": <uint16> }`

---

## Rule Providers

### `GET /providers/rules`

Retrieve all rule providers.

### `PUT /providers/rules/<name>`

Update a rule provider.

Response: HTTP 204

---

## Traffic / Memory / Logs (streaming)

### `GET /traffic`

Real-time traffic; pushed once per second.

| Field     | Type | Description                  |
| --------- | ---- | ---------------------------- |
| `up`      | int  | Current upload rate (bytes/s)|
| `down`    | int  | Current download rate (bytes/s)|
| `upTotal` | int  | Cumulative uploaded bytes    |
| `downTotal`| int  | Cumulative downloaded bytes  |

### `GET /memory`

Real-time memory usage; pushed once per second.

| Field    | Type | Description              |
| -------- | ---- | ------------------------ |
| `inuse`  | int  | Current memory in use (bytes) |
| `oslimit`| int  | OS memory limit (always 0) |

### `GET /logs`

Real-time logs. Also available as WebSocket.

Query:

| Parameter | Type   | Description                                       |
| --------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `level`   | string | `info`, `warning`, `error`, `debug`               |
| `format`  | string | `structured` for structured output (default: standard) |

Standard response (one JSON per line):

```json
{ "type": "info", "payload": "log message" }
```

Structured response:

```json
{ "time": "HH:MM:SS", "level": "info", "message": "…", "fields": [] }
```

---

## DNS

### `GET /dns/query`

Query DNS for a specified name and type.

Query: `?name=example.com&type=A`

Response: standard DNS message format (`Status`, `Question`, `TC`, `RD`, `RA`, `AD`, `CD`, `Answer`, `Authority`, `Additional`).

---

## Storage

### `GET /storage/<key>`

Retrieve a stored value. Returns `null` if the key does not exist.

### `PUT /storage/<key>`

Write a JSON value (maximum 1 MB).

Body: `{"foo": "bar"}`

Response: HTTP 204

### `DELETE /storage/<key>`

Delete a stored value.

Response: HTTP 204

---

## Restart / Upgrade

### `POST /restart`

Restart the mihomo kernel.

Body: `{"path": "", "payload": ""}`

Response: HTTP 204

### `POST /upgrade`

Update the kernel.

Query: `?channel=xxx&force=true`

Body: `{"path": "", "payload": ""}`

Response: `{ "status": "ok" }`

### `POST /upgrade/ui`

Update the external UI. Requires `external-ui` to be set.

Response: `{ "status": "ok" }`

### `POST /upgrade/geo`

Update the GEO database.

Body: `{"path": "", "payload": ""}`

Response: HTTP 204

---

## DEBUG

> Requires kernel started with `log-level: debug`.

### `PUT /debug/gc`

Perform active garbage collection.

Response: HTTP 204

### `GET /debug/pprof`

Open in browser for raw DEBUG information:

- `allocs` — memory allocation per function call
- `heap` — heap memory usage detail

Graphical reports via Graphviz:

```shell
go tool pprof -http=:8080 http://127.0.0.1:xxxx/debug/pprof/heap
go tool pprof -http=:8080 http://127.0.0.1:xxxx/debug/pprof/allocs
```

---

## Configuration Reference

### External Controller

```yaml
external-controller: 127.0.0.1:9090
secret: ""
external-controller-cors:
  allow-origins:
    - "*"
  allow-private-network: true
external-controller-unix: mihomo.sock
external-controller-pipe: \\.\pipe\mihomo
external-controller-tls: 127.0.0.1:9443
external-controller-routing-mark: 0
external-doh-server: /dns-query
```